From fe58ffd8868a64b268d3dffdd81455f510851838 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 19:51:32 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_tasks_panel: an Agent Tasks panel whose task history
 survives restarts

0037's card answers "what is running right now", and forgets: an ended task
leaves the card ten seconds later, and everything leaves it when Zeo quits.
Whether last night's build passed, or which subagent failed, was nowhere to
be read afterwards. This patch is the other half (story 014): a dockable
"Agent Tasks" panel listing every task the agent ran -- foreground and
background, live and finished, across every thread and every window -- kept
across restarts, and archivable.

The panel:

  * A crate of its own, agent_tasks_panel. The panel is "Agent Tasks", icon
    ListTodo, 320 px wide by default, docked left by default and movable to
    right or bottom. It toggles with agent_tasks_panel::ToggleFocus, bound in
    the Workspace context to ctrl-alt-shift-a on Linux and cmd-alt-shift-a on
    macOS (command palette: "agent tasks panel: toggle focus"). Not
    ctrl-alt-t, the first plan: upstream binds alt-ctrl-t to
    pane::CloseOtherItems in the Pane context, which shadows a Workspace
    binding whenever an editor has focus, and many Linux desktops grab that
    chord for a terminal.

  * Tasks are grouped by thread, threads ordered by their latest task, tasks
    newest first. Four filters -- Active, Finished, Failed, Archived -- with
    Active and Finished on by default; a toggle lasts for the session. A
    running row shows its live progress, read from whichever window's
    TasksCard holds the task, never from storage. Clicking a row opens its
    thread in the agent panel; a thread that no longer exists says so on the
    row instead of opening an empty one. Stop goes through the card's own
    request_stop, so it asks the same question 0037 asks. A finished task,
    or every finished task of a group, can be archived and unarchived; a
    running task cannot. Nothing is ever deleted automatically.

  * NO settings of its own -- no settings struct, nothing in default.json.
    The width persists with the workspace, as for every panel. The dock does
    not: the workspace saves a panel's dock only through that panel's
    settings, so this one keeps it in the key-value store under its panel key,
    "AgentTasksPanel". That key is global, so moving the panel in one window
    sets the dock for windows opened after it; an unreadable value falls back
    to left with a log line.

  * Loading never waits for the agent panel: zed.rs loads every panel in one
    join before the docks are restored, and with AI disabled the agent panel
    never appears. The card is attached when the agent panel is added, and
    re-attached when it is rebuilt; until then the panel shows the stored
    history and no live rows.

The history:

  * Its own sqlez domain, AgentTaskHistoryDb, one table keyed by (session id,
    task id). Not a table on ThreadMetadataDb, the obvious neighbour: sqlez
    migrations are positional per domain, and a changed entry aborts startup
    with "Migration changed for {domain} at step {index}". A migration
    appended to upstream's list would be overtaken by upstream's next one,
    and Zeo would stop opening. This list is the domain's alone, depends on
    no upstream domain, and is append-only: never edit an entry that has
    shipped, only add one after it. A database written before this patch
    gains the table on the first start.

  * Only the start and the outcome are written -- status, end time, tokens,
    tool uses. Progress while running is never stored.

  * The startup sweep: no task outlives the agent process that ran it, so
    every row still marked running when Zeo starts is marked interrupted,
    ending then. Activity heard while that sweep and the first load are in
    flight is queued and replayed after them, so a task started in the first
    frame is neither swept nor overwritten by the load. One ordered writer
    carries every write.

  * The storage cannot break startup. static_connection! never reports an
    open error: when the file cannot be opened, or any domain's migration
    fails, db::open_db logs it and falls back SILENTLY to a shared in-memory
    database. The store reads db::ALL_FILE_DB_FAILED -- not persistent(),
    which is false for test and ZED_STATELESS databases as well -- and marks
    the history unavailable: the panel shows "Task history is unavailable"
    with the cause above the live rows, writes are skipped, and Zeo runs as
    usual. A write that fails after a good open logs the session and task
    ids and keeps the in-memory state, so this session still shows the task.

Fed by the card -- the one change to 0037's code:

  * TasksCard now emits TaskActivity: Started once per task, Ended once per
    ending (one ending heard through two views of a session is one Ended,
    the rule 0037 already applies to the tray). A task first seen already
    ended gets a Started carrying its final status; a thread closed while a
    task runs ends that task as interrupted; and the card keeps emitting
    while disabled, hidden or minimized. It also emits ThreadTitleChanged,
    and the store moves every record of that session to the new title: a
    thread's first task is recorded before its title is generated, and was
    otherwise stored under the raw prompt.

  * agent_ui re-exports TaskActivity, TaskRecord, TasksCard and
    ThreadTitleChanged, and AgentPanel::tasks_card, test-only in 0037, is
    public. The store keeps a weak handle to every card it hears, so a task
    running in one window shows its progress, and Stop, in every window's
    panel.

The upstream touch is registration only, to keep each bump's refresh cheap:
the workspace member and dependency in Cargo.toml; the dependency in
crates/zed/Cargo.toml; agent_tasks_panel::init in crates/zed/src/main.rs,
after agent_ui::init, where app init lives; AgentTasksPanel::load joined with
the other panels in crates/zed/src/zed.rs; one line in each of the two
default keymaps. Cargo.lock gains the crate's own entry and one line in zed's
dependency list -- every dependency is a workspace crate or one already
locked, so no external crate is added.

Rides the claude-agent-acp-plus flag BY DEPENDENCY, like 0034, 0037 and 0038:
the panel is fed only by 0037's card, which lists only what this adapter
sends under _meta["_claude/tasks"] -- from claude-agent-acp-plus 0.24.0 on.
Without it the panel opens and records nothing. It also edits 0037's
tasks_card.rs, so it applies after 0038 and cannot ship without them.

zed's `test_action_namespaces` lists every action namespace and gains
`agent_tasks_panel` (added 2026-10-09; it had been failing since this patch
landed).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
